task-launcher (0.3.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4F.3 crash repair: the idle/auto-lock input tracker is installed
    on top-level windows instead of application-wide. An application-wide
    Python event filter made PySide wrap a QWebEngineUrlRequestJob during
    its C++ constructor, which segfaulted the launcher when the embedded
    Medical WebEngine reader opened a ZIM (reproduced on x86).
  * Medical passes a WebEngine crash guard to task-resources >= 0.2.4
    (~/.local/state/task-launcher/medical-webengine-guard.json). Works
    unchanged with task-resources 0.2.3 (no guard).

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0400

task-launcher (0.3.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4F.3 r2: Medical Refresh re-opens the Resources index (renews the
    read-only snapshot made by task-resources 0.2.3). Failure paths close
    the index connection and the reader; shutdown is idempotent. Suggests
    task-resources (>= 0.2.3).

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0400

task-launcher (0.3.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4F.3: the Medical view embeds T.A.S.K. Resources' own browser and
    ZIM reader in-process (task-resources >= 0.2.2): browsing, metadata,
    title/metadata and full-text search, embedded ZIM reading, back/forward,
    bookmarks; filtered to medical resources by default. The Resources index
    is opened read-only; bookmarks are kept in the launcher's private state
    file. Lock clears the content. No exec, no second process.

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0400

task-launcher (0.3.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4F.2: the Medical tile opens a native Medical view inside the
    launcher window (view stack with Back/Home) instead of the detached
    built-in window. It lists the T.A.S.K. Resources items in category
    "Medical" (index opened read-only, never reindexed) plus Kiwix/IIAB/folder
    items from the existing medical probe, with an empty state. Content
    opens in the Kiwix viewer, the desktop reader or T.A.S.K. Resources.
    Reopening reuses the single view. Legacy window kept as fallback.

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400

task-launcher (0.3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4F: Mesh tile shows a read-only unread badge (combined, per protocol
    Meshtastic/MeshCore, priority marker) from task-mesh-service's private
    socket or, failing that, the comms notification store opened read-only.
    The launcher never marks anything read. No other tile changes; all 12
    tiles and the task.medical / task.library ids are unchanged.

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:30:00 -0400

task-launcher (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the Library tile now starts task-resources when it is installed. In
    0.3.1 MainWindow.activate() exempted only "radio" from the native-window
    route, so Library always opened the built-in 4A viewer. The exemption now
    covers ("radio", "library"). Without task-resources the 4A viewer opens.
  * New regression tests drive the real shipped apps.d manifests through
    Registry + MainWindow.activate() (0.3.1 tested the registry only).
  * 050-library.toml unchanged.

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000

