task-launcher (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4C: T.A.S.K. branding only (the R.A.I.N. preset is a legacy alias);
    tile ids rain.* -> task.* with migration of saved order/hidden/enabled
    state (12 tiles kept); module status cards (task-mesh, task-aprs,
    task-sdr) in readiness; task-aprs / task-sdr / task-mesh preferred,
    legacy rain-mesh and the built-in receive-only APRS monitor as
    fallbacks, SDR++/Gqrx labelled External; Core socket /run/task first,
    /run/rain fallback.

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000

task-launcher (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4A. Tile ids and order unchanged; 0.1.0 user settings are read
    as is and never rewritten.
  * Manifest platform 0.2.0 (additive): readiness probes, status_note,
    [launch.labels], [[actions]]; new builtins library, radio, weather,
    medical. "Installed" is now shown as "Available".
  * Mesh Network launches rain-mesh when installed; otherwise Unavailable
    with a labelled temporary read-only status.
  * Maps & GPS: task-maps when present, else FoxtrotGPS labelled as the
    fallback; gpsmon/cgps actions in a terminal.
  * SDR: SDR++ or Gqrx; RTL-SDR readiness from the rain-core device list
    (display only); other SDR programs holding the dongle are flagged.
  * Early start failures show the exit code, time and last output line.
  * Native windows: Library (Kiwix discovery, collections, search,
    viewer), Radio / APRS (Direwolf status and a receive-only KISS
    monitor), Weather (local tools and data age, no forecast), Medical
    (offline reference finder, no records).
  * Background readiness probes, loopback only, with timeouts.
  * Maintainer email is a TODO placeholder until Joshua provides one.

 -- Joshua Sturtz <TODO-maintainer-email>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

task-launcher (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 3: first release. Native PySide6 launcher, manifest registry
